   \\[\n   b\\le n+1-a\\le n+1-(n-k+1)=k .\n   \\]\n\n   Hence \\(1\\le b\\le k\\).  Define  \n\n   \\[\n   i:=b\\;(\\in\\{1,\\dots ,k\\}).\n   \\]\n\n   For this \\(i\\) we have  \n\n   \\[\n   b = a + (i-1)\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad b = a + (b-1),\n   \\]\n\n   which is an identity; consequently \\((a,b)\\) lies on the sunny line \\(S_i\\).\n\n   Thus every lattice point with \\(a+b\\le n+1\\) belongs to at least one of the chosen lines.\n\n5. **Counting sunny lines.**  \n   The construction uses exactly the \\(k\\) lines \\(S_1,\\dots ,S_k\\), all of which are sunny, and the remaining \\(n-k\\) lines are vertical, hence non‑sunny.  Therefore the total number of sunny lines is precisely \\(k\\).\n\n6. **Conclusion.**  \n   For each integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) we have exhibited a set of \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering condition and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.  No other values of \\(k\\) are possible because the number of sunny lines cannot exceed the total number of lines, i.e. \\(k\\le n\\), and it cannot be negative.  Hence the admissible set of \\(k\\) is exactly \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,n\\}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{All integers }k\\text{ with }0\\le k\\le n\\text{ are possible}.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
