om \\(\\mathcal H\\cup\\mathcal V\\) and at least one line from \\(\\mathcal D\\); both are non\u2011sunny. Therefore  \n\n   \\[\n   k\\le n-2. \\tag{1}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Construction attaining every \\(k\\le n-2\\).**  \n\n   - Take the vertical line \\(\\ell_1:x=1\\) and the horizontal line \\(\\ell_2:y=1\\) (both non\u2011sunny).  \n   - For each integer \\(t\\) with \\(3\\le t\\le n\\) introduce the diagonal line  \n\n     \\[\n     d_t:\\;x+y=t\\qquad(\\text{slope }-1,\\text{ non\u2011sunny}).\n     \\]\n\n     The set  \n\n     \\[\n     \\mathcal L_0=\\{\\ell_1,\\ell_2\\}\\cup\\{d_t\\mid 3\\le t\\le n\\}\n     \\]\n\n     consists of \\(n-1\\) distinct non\u2011sunny lines and covers every point of \\(\\mathcal P_n\\).\n\n   - To obtain exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines, choose a subset \\(T\\subseteq\\{3,\\dots ,n\\}\\) of size \\(n-1-k\\).  \n     For each \\(t\\in T\\) pick an integer \\(c\\) with \\(1\\le c\\le t-1\\) and \\(c\\neq t-c\\) (possible because \\(t\\ge3\\)).  \n     Define the sunny line  \n\n     \\[\n     s_{t,c}:\\; y=\\frac{t-c}{c}\\,x + c .\n     \\]\n\n     Its slope \\(\\frac{t-c}{c}\\) is neither \\(0\\), \\(\\infty\\) nor \\(-1\\); the line passes through the two points \\((c,t-c)\\) and \\((t-c,c)\\), hence contains the whole diagonal \\(S_t\\).\n\n   - Replace each \\(d_t\\) with \\(t\\in T\\) by the corresponding sunny line \\(s_{t,c}\\).  \n     The resulting family  \n\n     \\[\n     \\mathcal L=\\{\\ell_1,\\ell_2\\}\\cup\\{d_t\\mid t\\notin T\\}\\cup\\{s_{t,c}\\mid t\\in T\\}\n     \\]\n\n     has exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines, \\(n\\) distinct lines, and still covers every required point (a point \\((a,b)\\) belongs to \\(S_t\\); if \\(t\\notin T\\) it lies on \\(d_t\\), otherwise on \\(s_{t,c}\\)).\n\n5. **Conclusion.**  \n   Inequality (1) shows that no configuration can have more than \\(n-2\\) sunny lines.  \n   The construction above shows that every integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) is attainable.  \n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n-2\\}} .\n\\]"
